      "generated_answer": "To calculate the joint resistance \\( R \\) of resistances connected in parallel, use the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{R} = \\frac{1}{R_1} + \\frac{1}{R_2} + \\frac{1}{R_3} + \\frac{1}{R_4} + \\frac{1}{R_5}\n\\]\n\nFor the given resistances (10, 15, 20, 25, 30 ohms), calculating gives:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{R} = \\frac{1}{10} + \\frac{1}{15} + \\frac{1}{20} + \\frac{1}{25} + \\frac{1}{30} = 0.1 + 0.0667 + 0.05 + 0.04 + 0.0333 = 0.29\n\\]\n\nThus, \\( R \\approx \\frac{1}{0.29} \\approx 3.45 \\) ohms, which rounds to about 3.46 ohms.\n\nTherefore, the answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\).",
