    "global index": "MMLUPro_health_4923",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A certain molecule acts by binding to cytochrome oxidase A3, the final enzyme in the electron transport chain. Administration of a large dose of this substance to a human would likely:\n\nOptions: \nA. Decrease the rate of glycolysis, leading to a drop in ATP production.\nB. Have no effect as cells would switch which macronutrient they metabolize to circumvent the blocked biochemical pathway.\nC. Stimulate the cell to increase its production of cytochrome oxidase A3 to compensate for the blocked enzyme.\nD. Lead to the overproduction of NADH, causing a buildup of toxic metabolites in the cell.\nE. Increase the cell’s ATP production as negative feedback would cause the cell to up-regulate anaerobic pathways.\nF. Increase the efficiency of the electron transport chain by providing an alternative pathway for electron transfer.\nG. Have no effect as the cells would increase their reliance on fatty acid oxidation for energy production.\nH. Lead to death due to an inability of the cell to pass electrons to oxygen, thus stopping aerobic respiration and asphyxiating the cells.\nI. Lead to death due to an inadequate supply of ADP to accept a phosphate group at the ATP synthase enzyme.\nJ. Cause a rapid increase in the production of reactive oxygen species, leading to oxidative stress and cell death.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The molecule described inhibits cytochrome oxidase A3, which is essential for transferring electrons to oxygen in the electron transport chain. This inhibition halts aerobic respiration, preventing ATP production and leading to cellular asphyxiation. The most likely outcome is cell death due to the complete blockage of oxygen utilization.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
