    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}\n\nThe context indicates that older persons with high financial assets (a proxy for higher socioeconomic status) accepted preventive home visits more frequently than those with low assets. This suggests that the acceptance rates of the national preventive home visit programme are socially imbalanced, with higher socioeconomic groups more likely to participate.",
      "success": true,
